  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 254 AM CDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nThe overall weather pattern persists through next week with a ridge \nto the west and a trough to the east and northwest flow aloft over \nthe Mississippi Valley.  The long wave trough does attenuate \nsomewhat in the Monday-Tuesday timeframe.  This allows the ridge to \nto drift eastward which brings warmer temperatures and higher \nhumidity back to the region.  This doesn't look like extreme heat, \njust more \"normal\" late August heat and humidity.  After another \ncool start to the day Monday, and highs in the low 80s, temperatures \nrise back into the mid and upper 80s through at least Wednesday or \nThursday. Deterministic guidance shows another short wave diving \nsouthwest from south central Canada into the Great Lakes region late \nin the week.  This pushes another cold front through the Mid \nMississippi Valley with the potential for some precip and perhaps \ncooler temperatures for Friday.  However, the LREF cluster analysis \nis showing variance in both the amplitude and speed of the late-week \nshort wave.  The timing and strength of the cold front along with \nthe chance for precip that it brings is therefore questionable. Have \nleft NBM temps and PoPs alone for the end of the week, which keeps \nhighs in the mid to upper 80s and only sporadic slight chance PoPs.",
